node scripts/log-summary.mjs [--since <ISO date>] [file]
\`\`\`

Summarizes a JSONL event log: counts per level plus the first and last timestamps. \`--since\`
keeps only events at or after the given instant — any \`Date.parse\`-able value, such as
\`2026-01-04\` or \`2026-01-04T09:06:00Z\`. While \`--since\` is active, events without a \`time\`
field are dropped. An unparseable or missing date exits 1 with a message on stderr. The file
defaults to \`fixtures/events.jsonl\`.`,
  }],
